21,22 $ Apothecia not dark brown, without lilaceous tones; Asia, Europe or North America
22,0 $ Medullary excipulum with reddish brown resinous exudates scattered among and covering some hyphae; ectal excipulum of textura prismatica to textura intricata; receptacle surface with contrasting brown warts $O. papillata 6. 
22,23 $ Medullary excipulum sometimes with yellowish brown resinous exudates at septa, not covering hyphae; ectal excipulum of textura angularis; receptacle surface with contrasting warts or not
23,0 $ At least some warts higher than 85 µm ; basal tomentum orange-ochre when dried; apothecial sections often yellow in KOH; without resinous exudates at septa in the medullary excipulum $ O. tuomikoskii 9
23,24 $ Warts up to 85 µm ; basal tomentum pale ochre or yellow when dried; apothecial sections not yellow in KOH; sometimes with resinous exudates at septa in the medullary excipulum
24,25 $ Hymenium with distinct yellow or orange tones, ochreyellow to pinkish orange; resinous exudates on the ectal excipulum partly dissolving into reddish grey, heterogeneous drops in KOH or basal mycelium yellow in KOH .
24,26 $ Hymenium without or with weak orange tones; resinous exudates sometimes turning reddish brown but not dissolving into drops in KOH; basal mycelium not turning yellow in KOH
25,0 $ Resinous exudates on the ectal excipulum partly dissolving into reddish grey heterogeneous drops in KOH; basal mycelium not turning yellow in KOH; North America $ O. pseudoleporina 8. 
25,0 $ Resinous exudates on the ectal excipulum not dissolving into reddish grey heterogeneous drops in KOH; basal mycelium turning yellow in KOH; Asia $ O. brevispora 19. 
26,0 $ Hymenium sometimes with pink tones; apothecia yellowish ochre to brown; narrowly ear-shaped in the beginning $ O. nannfeldtii 14. 
26,27 $ Hymenium without pink tones; apothecia reddish brown to orange-brown; broadly ear-shaped
27,0 $ Spores Lm = 10-10.7 µm ; Qm = 1.6-1.7 $ O. formicarum 13. 
27,0 $ Spores Lm = 11.1-11.7 µm ; Qm = 1.7-1.9 $ O. subformicarum 15. 
28,29 $ Spores Qm < 1.8; ear-shaped
28,30 $ Spores Qm > 1.8; ear- or cup-shaped
29,0 $ Apothecia dark brown, sometimes with olivaceous tint; paraphyses mostly with distinct notches . $O. brunneoparva 10
29,0 $ Apothecia cinnamon brown, without olivaceous tint; paraphyses not or slightly notched $ O. leporina 7. 
30,0 $ Apothecia ochraceous yellow, hymenium often with pink tones; basal mycelium turning yellow in KOH $ O. onotica 22
30,31 $ Apothecia pale or dark brown, without pink tones; basal mycelium not turning yellow in KOH
31,0 $ Receptacle medium brown; ectal excipulum resinous exudates absent or scarce, light yellowish brown; basal mycelium without dark brown resinous exudates $O. alutacea s.l. 5
31,32 $ Receptacle dark purple brown; ectal excipulum resinous exudates abundant, dark brown; basal mycelium with dark brown resinous exudates
32,0 $ Spores Qm < 2, ellipsoid; apothecia mostly ear-shaped; North America $ O. smithii 24. 
32,33 $ Spores Qm > 2, ellipsoid-fusoid; apothecia mostly cupshaped, split; Eurasia and North America
33,0 $ Receptacle strikingly purple-violaceous (fresh); medullary excipulum without, or rarely with flabellate crystal-like exudates, forming cross-like aggregates; under conifers on calcareous ground $ O. mirabilis 21. 
33,0 $ Receptacle mostly without purple tones; medullary excipulum with striate exudates covering some hyphae, sometimes forming crystal-like aggregates; often under deciduoustrees or on acidic ground $ O. bufonia 20.
